 \section{Conclusion}
-With graph computation and generated code held fixed, an associated-label intervention can cause an actual generated Android getter to fail after inference; a count-preserving permutation can instead succeed while changing the exposed association. The official Task classifier enforces the tested cardinality condition earlier, while the secondary Hand Task is insensitive to the tested output-metadata exchange on its prescribed input. These observations support separate reporting of structural acceptance, reference-backed association agreement, and selected-consumer compatibility, with intervention preservation checked separately. They provide bounded executable evidence for these distinctions and a supporting pre-flight method with explicit abstention.
